Use Qt5.15/Qt6 common APIs for GUI DPI and font measurements.

QDesktopWidget is removed in Qt6, even unused includes break compilation.
Initialize the same integer primary-screen DPI from QScreen's rounded
logicalDotsPerInchX/Y values and remove obsolete includes.
QFontMetrics::horizontalAdvance replaces the removed width method.
The layout margins retain their existing values on both toolkits.  Replace
the removed QAbstractItemView::viewOptions() with initViewItemOption()
under Qt6, keeping the Qt5 viewOptions() semantics as view-level option
initialization.
Use QStyleOption::initFrom instead of the removed init alias, preserving
widget-derived palette, geometry and state for slider and splash painting.
Size expanding line editors from CT_LineEdit under Qt6, retaining the custom
globalStrut content floor on Qt5 where that application API still exists.
Map tablet cursor, eraser and pen labels through QPointingDevice on Qt6,
retaining the Qt5 labels and the existing application pen-type mapping.

Shortcut composition uses bitwise OR: modifier flags must precede the key
and the combination is Qt::CTRL | Qt::Key_X rather than integer addition,
which Qt6 rejects for key sequences.
Upstream: Qt6 portability for pinned 3763d805d7d277d10af10025ae41af677682b3e6.

Qt containers return qsizetype; mixing them with int arguments in std::min
and std::max no longer compiles.  Size comparisons are performed in the wide
type, and each value is bounded before the single cast that narrows it to
int for its bounded int consumers (recent-file count, path-component loop
count).

